12
00:49:53,684 --> 00:49:59,684
Clean, Shaven is a 1993 drama film written, produced and directed by Lodge Kerrigan, in which Peter Winter (played by Peter
Greene) is a man with schizophrenia desperately trying to get his daughter back from her adoptive mother.

13
00:54:03,157 --> 00:54:09,157
The film attempts to subjectively view schizophrenia
and those who are affected by it.

14
00:58:12,631 --> 00:58:18,631
At the 1993 Chicago Film Festival, the film won the
Silver Hugo Award for Best First Feature.

15
01:02:22,105 --> 01:02:28,105
The film was screened in the Un Certain Regard section and nominated for
the Caméra d'Or award at the 1994 Cannes Film Festival.

16
01:06:31,578 --> 01:06:37,578
Clean, Shaven was made a part of The Criterion Collection in 2006.

17
01:10:41,052 --> 01:10:47,052
The film explores themes of daughter, beach,
schizophrenia, obsession, detective.

18
01:14:50,526 --> 01:14:56,526
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and intense.
